course: dictionary
lesson: 9881
title: A tad: meaning a little
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «A tad» means a small amount, or a little. «Can I have a tad of milk?» asks for only a small splash. It is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing.
explain: Put «a tad» before an adjective or adverb and it means slightly. «The soup was a tad cold» means it was a bit cold, not frozen. To check, swap in «a little». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: People also use «a tad» to sound modest or polite. «It's a tad expensive» may mean it is very expensive, because the speaker is softening what they say. Look at the other clues in the sentence to work out how strong the meaning really is.
fact: «A tad» is informal, so it belongs to everyday speech more than to formal writing.
fact: «A tad» means a small amount: «a tad of milk» is only a splash.
fact: «A tad» before an adjective means slightly: «a tad cold» means a little cold.
fact: «Tad» was also old US slang for a small child, especially a boy.
fact: Words close in meaning to «a tad» include «a smidge», «a touch», «a bit» and «slightly».
exercise: «Can I have a tad of milk in my tea?» What does a tad of milk mean? | Milk that has gone sour | A full bottle | A large jug | *A small amount
exercise: «The soup was a tad cold.» What does a tad cold mean? | Freezing solid | Cold enough to snow | Warm and steaming | *Slightly cold
exercise: Mia says «It's a tad expensive» about a new bike. Why might she say it that way? | Because the bike is free | Because the bike is very small | Because tad means bicycle | *To sound modest, when it may really cost a lot
test: «There is a tad of cake left.» What does a tad of cake mean? | *A small piece | A whole cake | Cake that has gone stale | Plenty of cake
test: Which word means nearly the same as «a tad» in «a tad late»? | Yesterday | *A touch | Very early | Never
exam: Tom says «The film was a tad scary» about a film that gave him nightmares. What does a tad scary suggest? | Not scary at all | The film was scary only in a tiny room | The film was short | *He is playing down how scary it really was
